164
00:18:02,460 --> 00:18:09,460
In the book of John, Jesus heals a man who was born blind.

165
00:18:10,460 --> 00:18:19,460
And when Jesus's enemies heard about this, they harassed this man who could now see.

166
00:18:19,460 --> 00:18:24,460
And eventually they kicked him out of his synagogue.

167
00:18:25,460 --> 00:18:31,460
It was a big deal because it brought disgrace on his family.

168
00:18:31,460 --> 00:18:34,460
It meant he couldn't go to church anymore.

169
00:18:34,460 --> 00:18:39,460
And it pretty much meant that he could never live a normal life in the community that he grew up in.

170
00:18:42,460 --> 00:18:51,460
It almost made him invisible to the people that he now lived with, which is ironic because he was blind for so long.

171
00:18:51,460 --> 00:18:57,460
And now they wouldn't really be seeing him the same way as they saw everyone else.

172
00:18:59,460 --> 00:19:00,460
That's pretty dark.

173
00:19:00,460 --> 00:19:04,460
Jesus heard about this and he searched for the man that he found him.

174
00:19:04,460 --> 00:19:07,460
He went out after him and he found him.

175
00:19:09,460 --> 00:19:10,460
And the man believed Jesus.

176
00:19:10,460 --> 00:19:14,460
He believed the gospel just like many of us have.

177
00:19:14,460 --> 00:19:25,460
A lot of us, we've learned about Jesus, how he accepted our punishment and how he died in our place.

178
00:19:26,460 --> 00:19:38,460
We've learned that we are acquitted, that we're declared innocent of the fatal consequences of our sins and our failures.

179
00:19:38,460 --> 00:19:49,460
And we've moved from that understanding to an acceptance that what Jesus did applies to us.

180
00:19:50,460 --> 00:19:57,460
That we're the ones he came to find, that we're the ones whose sin can be taken away.

181
00:19:57,460 --> 00:20:02,460
We move from that acceptance to a commitment.

182
00:20:02,460 --> 00:20:07,460
To living according to Jesus' teachings.

183
00:20:07,460 --> 00:20:19,460
